{"name":"Aqua Nation","hex":"#08787f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aqua","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water (as a compound).","A shade of colour, usually a mix of blue and green, most often similar to the colour cyan, though also sometimes closer to turquoise or aquamarine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aqua"},{"term":"nation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A historically constituted, stable community of people, formed based on a common economic life, ethnicity, language, religion, and/or territory, and manifested in a common culture.","A community united by some trait (especially an interest) but not historically constituted."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Damnation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aqua (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua was a Danish eurodance band, best known for their 1997 single \"Barbie Girl\". The group formed in 1995 in Copenhagen and achieved international success around the world in the late 1990s and early 2000s. The band released three albums: Aquarium in 1997, Aquarius in 2000 and Megalomania in 2011. The group sold an estimated 33 million albums and singles, making them the most profitable Danish band ever."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Aqua_performing_at_Caesars_Windsor%2C_Windsor%2C_Ontario%2C_2025-09-26_30.jpg/330px-Aqua_performing_at_Caesars_Windsor%2C_Windsor%2C_Ontario%2C_2025-09-26_30.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(band)","wikidata":"Q213388"},{"title":"Aqua (Asia album)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is the fourth studio album by British rock supergroup Asia, released in 1992. It was the first album with longtime vocalist and bassist John Payne."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/12/Asia_-_Aqua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(Asia_album)","wikidata":"Q622874"},{"title":"Nation","blocks":[{"text":"A nation is a type of social organization where a collective identity—a national identity—has emerged from a combination of shared features across a given population, such as language, history, ethnicity, culture, territory, and society. Some nations are constructed around ethnicity while others are bound by political constitutions."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nation","wikidata":"Q6266"},{"title":"Aqua (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a variation of the color cyan. The normalized color coordinates for the two web colors named aqua and cyan are identical. It was one of the three secondary colors of the RGB color model used on computer and television displays. In the HSV color wheel aqua is precisely halfway between blue and green. However, aqua is not the same as the primary subtractive color named process cyan used in printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/330px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(color)","wikidata":"Q372733"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Aqua_Gron_Concert_2008.jpg/500px-Aqua_Gron_Concert_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Aqua_Gron_Concert_2008.jpg/500px-Aqua_Gron_Concert_2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aqua at the Grøn Koncert in 2008 (from left: Rasted, Dif, Nystrøm, Norreen)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAqua_Gron_Concert_2008.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo